**What changed:** Angular 20.3.0 removed the module-level global platform injector from the server-side rendering bootstrapping flow, replacing it with a per-request `BootstrapContext` passed to `bootstrapApplication`, so each server render gets an isolated platform injector and cannot leak state between concurrent requests (https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/63636, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/angular/angular/20.3.0/CHANGELOG.md). Custom server bootstrap functions in `main.server.ts` must now accept the context and forward it as the third argument: before `const bootstrap = () => bootstrapApplication(AppComponent, config);`, after `const bootstrap = (context: BootstrapContext) => bootstrapApplication(AppComponent, config, context);` (20.3.0 CHANGELOG). The change shipped as `feat(core): introduce BootstrapContext for improved server bootstrapping` (#63636, commit `8bf80c9d2314b4f2bcf3df83ae01552a6fc49834`) (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/8bf80c9d2314b4f2bcf3df83ae01552a6fc49834). Also, `getPlatform()` now returns `null` and `destroyPlatform()` is a no-op when running in a server environment (20.3.0 CHANGELOG).

**Affects:** SSR/hybrid apps with a custom `main.server.ts` bootstrap function (or any code calling `bootstrapApplication` manually on the server), and code calling `getPlatform()` / `destroyPlatform()` on the server.

**Action:** required: update the `main.server.ts` bootstrap function to take a `BootstrapContext` parameter and pass it as the third argument to `bootstrapApplication`, or run the provided schematic, which "automatically update[s] `main.server.ts` files to pass the `BootstrapContext` to the `bootstrapApplication` call" (20.3.0 CHANGELOG); re-verify any server-side use of `getPlatform()`/`destroyPlatform()`, which no longer report/destroy a platform in a server environment.

**Before/after:**
```ts
// Before:
const bootstrap = () => bootstrapApplication(AppComponent, config);

// After:
const bootstrap = (context: BootstrapContext) =>
  bootstrapApplication(AppComponent, config, context);
```

**What changed:** The server bootstrapping process no longer uses a module-level global platform injector. A new `BootstrapContext` interface (with a `platformRef: PlatformRef` member, exported from `@angular/platform-browser`) is passed as a third argument to `bootstrapApplication`, and `renderApplication`'s `bootstrap` callback now takes `(context: BootstrapContext)` instead of `()` (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/6117ccee2e1507fb00549cd70e064282645db803). New signature: `bootstrapApplication(rootComponent, options?, bootstrapContext?)` (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/8bf80c9d2314b4f2bcf3df83ae01552a6fc49834.patch). Additionally, `getPlatform()` now returns `null` and `destroyPlatform()` is a no-op in a server environment. A schematic `add-bootstrap-context-to-server-main` is provided (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/8bf80c9d2314b4f2bcf3df83ae01552a6fc49834.patch).

**Affects:** Applications that server-render using `@angular/platform-server`, i.e. those with a `main.server.ts` exporting a bootstrap function calling `bootstrapApplication`, or that call `renderApplication`, or rely on `getPlatform()`/`destroyPlatform()` on the server.

**Action:** required: update `main.server.ts` so the exported bootstrap arrow function accepts a `BootstrapContext` parameter and passes it as the third argument to `bootstrapApplication`; import `BootstrapContext` from `@angular/platform-browser`; re-verify `renderApplication` callers and any code relying on `getPlatform()`/`destroyPlatform()` in server environments. The `add-bootstrap-context-to-server-main` schematic performs these `main.server.ts` edits automatically.

**Before/after:**
```ts
// Before
import {bootstrapApplication} from '@angular/platform-browser';
const bootstrap = () => bootstrapApplication(AppComponent, config);

// After
import {bootstrapApplication, BootstrapContext} from '@angular/platform-browser';
const bootstrap = (context: BootstrapContext) =>
  bootstrapApplication(AppComponent, config, context);
```
```ts
// renderApplication
export function renderApplication(bootstrap: (context: BootstrapContext) => Promise<ApplicationRef>, options: {
    document?: string | Document;
    url?: string;
    platformProviders?: Provider[];
```
